  "lineage": "Volga-Tatar tradition of Kazan and the middle Volga, collected from the 1920s by Soltan Gabashi and Ghazi Almuhammetov and issued through Soviet Melodiya and Tatar Radio — anhemitonic pentatonic melodies, long ornamented ozyn köy lyric songs in free rhythm, brisk 2/4 kyska köy dance songs, the quray reed flute and kubyz jaw harp, and after the 19th century the talyanka button accordion carrying both melody and chordal pulse.",
